  "about": "Problem 4 smoke test. Claude Code (the vibe coder) answered one plain-English question per ticket by calling the campus-customs MCP server through .mcp.json. Each entry has the prompt, the tool Claude Code chose, the tool output, and a check of every output value against data/campus_customs_new.db.",
  "how_tested": [
    "Claude Code 2.1.246 ran each prompt headless, loading the project's .mcp.json with --mcp-config. Exact command: CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1 claude -p --input-format stream-json --replay-user-messages --output-format stream-json --verbose --mcp-config .mcp.json --strict-mcp-config --tools '' --allowedTools mcp__campus-customs__check_stock_and_price mcp__campus-customs__check_invoice mcp__campus-customs__check_lease --no-session-persistence --max-turns 4 --model sonnet < prompt-as-stream-json-user-message",
    "Built-in tools were off (--tools \"\"), so the three campus-customs tools were the only tools; the prompts ask business questions and do not name a tool, so Claude Code picked the tool and its arguments.",
    "Each prompt was sent on stdin and replayed into the transcript, so the recorded prompt is the one the run received. Auto-memory was off so the run only answered its prompt.",
    "tool_output is the tool result exactly as Claude Code passed it to the model (whole numbers such as 840.0 show as 840).",
    "db_check recomputes every value in tool_output with SQL run read-only on data/campus_customs_new.db (the queries and rows are included), separately from mcp_server/server.py, and checks that the arguments came from the ticket row.",
    "An earlier batch, with prompts that nearly named the tools and with memory on, returned the same tool outputs; it was replaced by this batch."
